{
 "_about": "Read by scripts/links.py and scripts/chrome.py. 'rewrites' are permanent: a link to the key path now points at the value (the old path is retired or is a 301 alias in netlify.toml). 'rewrite_self' is what a rewrite becomes when its target is the page the link sits on: a pending span to the listed real target. 'targets' gives the truthful fallback for a promised page that is not built yet; an empty string means no truthful fallback exists and the anchor becomes a pending span. Targets not listed fall back by class: a metro to its state page's #metros, a subtype to its hub. A fallback that would be the page itself becomes a span. 'folded' lists promised pages that WEB-FSC-6 folded into a section of their parent (the targets give the section): build.py writes every link to such a section as a pending link to the promised page, so links.py --relink restores it the day a lane builds that page.",
